### msvcservice — walk the reference order flow (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client).
### Local runs need no token: the development overlay accepts header identities.
@host = http://localhost:8080
# probes and /metrics live on the admin listener, not on the API
@admin = http://localhost:8081
@consumer = X-Dev-Subject: 1
@realm = X-Dev-Realm: CONSUMER

### probes & metrics (admin listener)
GET {{admin}}/health/startup
###
GET {{admin}}/health/live
###
GET {{admin}}/health/ready
###
GET {{admin}}/metrics

### unauthenticated → 401 problem details
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders

### create an order (the inventory service prices it via WireMock → outbox → RabbitMQ → consumer confirms it)
### there is no unitPrice in the request: prices are never the client's to state
# @name create
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-0001

{ "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 2 } ] }

### same key again → replayed response, Idempotency-Replayed: true
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}
Idempotency-Key: demo-0001

{ "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 2 } ] }

### read it back (cached) — status flips to CONFIRMED once the consumer ran
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{create.response.body.id}}
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

### my orders, paged
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders?page=1&pageSize=10
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

### validation → 400 VALIDATION_FAILED with the errors map
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

{ "items": [ { "sku": "", "quantity": 0 } ] }

### a well-formed body that breaks a rule of the order → 422 ORDER_ITEMS_REQUIRED (ORDER_ITEM_INVALID past 100 items)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

{ "items": [] }

### an id that is not a positive integer → 400 BAD_REQUEST
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders/abc
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

### business rule → 422 ORDER_ITEM_UNAVAILABLE (WireMock stub)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

{ "items": [ { "sku": "OUT-OF-STOCK", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### downstream fault → 502 UPSTREAM_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE (and the breaker opens after 5 in a row)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

{ "items": [ { "sku": "FAULT", "quantity": 1 } ] }

### cancel a CONFIRMED order → 409 ORDER_NOT_CANCELLABLE
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/orders/{{create.response.body.id}}
{{consumer}}
{{realm}}

### wrong plane → 403 (a back-office identity on a consumer route)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders
X-Dev-Subject: 1
X-Dev-Realm: BACKOFFICE
X-Dev-Scopes: orders.read

### back office: every customer's orders, newest first, by cursor (needs the orders.read scope);
### pass the response's nextCursor as ?cursor= for the next page
GET {{host}}/api/v1/backoffice/orders?limit=5
X-Dev-Subject: 7
X-Dev-Realm: BACKOFFICE
X-Dev-Scopes: orders.read

### a real token, minted like user-svc's: tools/mint-dev-token.sh --sub 1 --realm CONSUMER
GET {{host}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer <paste the token here>
